==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-lighten up.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|intransitive|transitive}} To make (something) or to become less [[serious]] and more [[cheerful]] or [[casual]]; to [[relax]].
#: {{cot|en|chill out}}
#: {{ux|en|I wish he'd '''lighten up''' a bit and realize that we were only joking.}}
#: {{ux|en|The mood at work has been tense, so he's looking for ways to '''lighten''' it '''up'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=6 Aug 83 |journal=Gay Community News|page=8|author=Michael Bronski|title=Gay Sensibility, Straight Imitation|text=Sondheim's sense of life — which is pretty pessimistic (I don't think that anyone ever ends happily ever after in a Sondheim musical) — is brought through without trying to '''lighten it up'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=w:Adele|title=First Love
|passage=you '''lighten up''' my heart when I start to cry}}
# {{senseid|en|decrease the weight of (something)}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[lighten]] (something): to decrease its [[weight]].
#: {{nearsyn|en|slim down}}
#: {{ux|en|He can't get any more power out of it [his drag racer], so now he's looking for ways to '''lighten''' it '''up'''.}}
